[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2565160083","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100917#issuecomment-2565160083","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100917","id":2565160083,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y5TyT","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-30T08:21:01Z","updated_at":"2024-12-30T08:29:35Z","body":"The reason drag does not work here is because you are replacing the entire mesh and redrawing the full resource inspector. So basically what you try to drag you remove. You just don't see it because it gets replaced so quickly.\n\nWhen you use the `ArrayMesh.surface_update_vertex_region` you are actually only updating data parts of the existing Mesh which is why it works.\n\nYou would need to use a custom inspector that can keep your properties and does not target the resource directly. You can't use the generic resource inspector when the resource gets replaced on changes. E.g. Skeleton3D and others all use custom inspectors for this very reason. This is an older issue that I have seen before around here so there are some duplicates to find.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2565160083/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2565235371","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100917#issuecomment-2565235371","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100917","id":2565235371,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y5mKr","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-30T09:29:42Z","updated_at":"2024-12-30T09:32:22Z","body":"> The reason drag does not work here is because you are replacing the entire mesh and redrawing the full resource inspector. So basically what you try to drag you remove. You just don't see it because it gets replaced so quickly.\n> \n> When you use the `ArrayMesh.surface_update_vertex_region` you are actually only updating data parts of the existing Mesh which is why it works.\n> \n> You would need to use a custom inspector that can keep your properties and does not target the resource directly. You can't use the generic resource inspector when the resource gets replaced on changes. E.g. Skeleton3D and others all use custom inspectors for this very reason. This is an older issue that I have seen before around here so there are some duplicates to find.\n\nI'm not understanding why recreating a surface in an `ArrayMesh` would replace the entire resource. Why is that necessary?\nAlso not understanding the `Skeleton3D` comparison because that's a node, not a resource. Although I am aware that it uses custom inspector logic, I think it's because Skeleton3D doesn't really store _properties_ at all, it just exposes methods to access the underlying data store. The custom inspector does the same.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2565235371/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2565242876","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100917#issuecomment-2565242876","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100917","id":2565242876,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y5n_8","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-30T09:37:16Z","updated_at":"2024-12-30T09:37:16Z","body":"UPDATE: Replacing the calls with the `RenderingServer` equivalents does _not_ cause this bug! 😲\n```gdscript\nRenderingServer.mesh_clear(get_rid())\nRenderingServer.mesh_add_surface_from_arrays(get_rid(), RenderingServer.PRIMITIVE_TRIANGLES, arrays)\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2565242876/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2565274293","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100917#issuecomment-2565274293","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100917","id":2565274293,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y5vq1","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-30T10:08:36Z","updated_at":"2024-12-30T10:08:36Z","body":"**UPDATE 2**:\nIt seems like the culprit is `notify_property_list_changed()` being called in `ArrayMesh`'s native methods.\nSo this is a general issue of mouse control being taken away whenever the inspector has to be rebuilt as a consequence of `notify_property_list_changed()`. As such, I think this bug can be closed. I'm not sure if this is fully avoidable, but at least there's the workaround of using the `RenderingServer`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2565274293/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2565570621","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100917#issuecomment-2565570621","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100917","id":2565570621,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y64A9","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-30T14:43:36Z","updated_at":"2024-12-30T14:43:36Z","body":"To add to this yes `notify_property_list_changed()` causes a redraw of the resource inspector and since a mesh has a lot of \"dynamic\" properties for the surfaces a new drawn resource inspector has no track of the old slider that was e.g. dragged so the focus and input gets lost.\n\nSkeleton3D was just one example for a custom inspector and why a simple resource inspector often does not work for more complex things. E.g. something touches a bone transform and the entire skeleton inspector would need to redraw. That would be even worse than this issue here with the ArrayMesh.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2565570621/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]